Hi again!

I would like to refine my question.

So when action button is pressed.

output$table <- renderDataTable({
   if (input$searchAction == 0) return()

   if (input$search_result == "Please search first" || input$search_result == 0) return()

   data <- get_business_data()
   data
 },option=list(iDisplayLength=10,
               bAutoWidth=FALSE,
               aoColumns=NULL,
               aoColumnDefs = list(list(sWidth="7em",
                                        aTargets=c(list(0),list(1))))))

This code is run because it depends on all 3 inputs I stated.
However, when the action button is pressed for the first time, it DOESN'T react because I put the argument there.
Am I correct here?

I want the above code to get executed, when Action button is not clicked, but input$search_result is changed
Right now, when action button is clicked, business list gets updated which changes input$search_result which then triggers the above code.

Is something like this possible? I think I am not totally understanding observe and isolate and its best uses yet either.

Looking forward to your answer!

